w: Praise, my soul, the King of hea- ven; To His feet thy tri- bute bring.
w: Praise Him for His grace and fa- vor To our fa- thers in dis- tress.
w: Fa- ther like He tends and spares us; Well our fee- ble frame He knows.
w: Frail as sum- mer's flower we flour- ish, Blows the wind and it is gone;
w: An- gels, help us to a- dore Him; Ye be- hold Him face to face;
